  "narrative": "The new evidence mostly provides negative specificity and context checks around the central accepted effects. For the constructed markers, H17/R53, H18/R54, H19/R55, H21/R56, H22/R57, and H23/R58 are all small and imprecise. Their signed estimates are near zero, and the 95% upper bounds are roughly 0.028-0.060, below the approximate 0.1 dependency-score benchmark I am using to distinguish trivial from scientifically meaningful associations. These nulls do not create scientific claims; they instead suggest that the large WRN/SMARCA2/NFE2L2 associations are not tracking arbitrary marker-positive groups. I therefore reject the registered marker main-effect and marker-interaction claims as completed negative controls and close them. \n\nThe culture interaction results are mixed but mostly reassuring. H32/R60 for SMARCA2 and H33/R61 for NFE2L2 are null, with upper bounds 0.0596 and 0.0391, below the practical benchmark; I reject those as meaningful modifiers of the validated SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 and accepted KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 relationships. H31/R59 for MSI-high/WRN is the only borderline culture result: the signed interaction is +0.114 with 95% interval [0.041, 0.187]. The point estimate is above the benchmark, but the lower bound is below it, so I leave H31 unresolved and deferred rather than accepting a clinically meaningful culture modification. Importantly, this borderline interaction does not invalidate the independently validated H11 MSI-high/WRN association, because the adherent-culture main effect remains extremely large at R30 = +0.816 [0.784, 0.849]. \n\nThe STK11 checks also support specificity of the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 relationship. H69/R62 tests whether STK11 loss modifies the KEAP1-loss contrast; the signed estimate is -0.029 [-0.088, 0.030], so the upper bound is well below the benchmark and the registered direction is unsupported. H70/R63 tests STK11 loss alone against NFE2L2 dependency; the signed estimate is -0.023 [-0.065, 0.018], again null. I reject H69 and H70 as completed checks and close them. The MSI-high/STK11 interaction H71/R64 is uninformative because the MSI-high and STK11-loss interaction cell has only 19 observations and the Welch analysis is invalid. I leave H71 unresolved but close it because this exact stratification is underpowered and future effort should go to independent validation of H13. \n\nI am requesting independent validation for H13, KEAP1 loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency. This is the largest accepted but unvalidated effect. The main discovery association is R7 = +0.797 [0.776, 0.819], and it is supported by context effects in adenocarcinoma R16 = +0.795, Ky library R29 = +0.787, and adherent culture R32 = +0.795. The new robustness checks reduce concern that the KEAP1/NFE2L2 association is explained by marker-D assay artifacts, culture environment, or STK11 co-alteration: marker D direct and interaction effects are null, culture interaction is null, and STK11 direct and interaction effects are null. This does not establish causality or clinical generalizability, but it makes H13 the best next candidate for independent validation. All accepted associations remain dataset-specific statistical associations. \n\nFrom a critical-reviewer perspective, the main threats are multiplicity and correlated genomic co-alterations. I am not accepting the borderline H31 culture interaction because its interval includes clinically trivial effects, and I am treating marker D/E/F tests as arbitrary-assay controls rather than biological pathways. The central validated claims H11, H12, and H48 remain distinct from the exploratory negative controls.",
  "research_notes": "Validated associations: H11 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H12 SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H48 TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 dependency. Main accepted unvalidated target: H13 KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; request validation now. H13 support: discovery R7 +0.797 [0.776,0.819], adenocarcinoma R16, Ky library R29, adherent culture R32; new null specificity checks: marker D direct/interaction H23/H19, culture interaction H33, STK11 direct/interaction H70/H69. \n\nThis batch rejects marker controls H17/H18/H19/H21/H22/H23 as small and bounded below the practical ~0.1 benchmark. H31 WRN culture interaction R59 +0.114 [0.041,0.187] is borderline: unresolved/deferred, does not overturn validated H11 because adherent main effect R30 is huge. H32/H33 culture interactions are null; rejected. H69/H70 STK11 NFE2L2 checks null; rejected. H71 MSI-STK11 interaction invalid due small cell; closed unresolved. \n\nNext priorities: assess H13 independent validation when delivered; then consider CDKN2A/USP7/MDM2 checks H85/H86/H88, MYC interaction H87, BRCA2 tests H83/H73/H74, pathway receptor tests H77-H82, TMED10 H49/H68. Avoid overinterpreting constructed markers. All results are associations in supplied dataset/validation structure.",
